/****** autodoc.datatype/std/DT_MakeClass ******************************************************************
*
*   NAME
*	Autodoc_New -- Create a new Autodoc datatype object.
*
*   SYNOPSIS
*	Object *obj = NewObjectA(NULL, "autodoc.datatype", DTA_Name, name, TAG_DONE);
*
*   FUNCTION
*	Creates a new Autodoc datatype object, initializing a memory pool
*	for line layout. The underlying text.datatype superclass handles
*	buffer management and rendering; this class only adds Autodoc
*	aware line layout.
*
*   INPUTS
*	name         - The name of the Autodoc file being viewed.
*
*   RESULT
*	obj          - A new object, or NULL on failure.
*
*   EXAMPLE
*	/*
*	Object *obj = NewObjectA(NULL, "autodoc.datatype",
*	                           DTA_Name, (IPTR)name,
*	                           TAG_DONE);
*	if (obj) DoMethod(obj, DTM_PROCLAYOUT, NULL);
*	*/
*
*   NOTES
*	Requires datatypes.library and text.datatype to be installed.
*	Memory pool size is estimated from the buffer length.
*
*   BUGS
*	None known.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*	DT_MakeClass(), Autodoc_AsyncLayout()
*
******* autodoc.datatype/std/Autodoc_AsyncLayout ************************************************************
*
*   NAME
*	Autodoc_AsyncLayout -- Lay out Autodoc text into line segments.
*
*   SYNOPSIS
*	ULONG total = Autodoc_AsyncLayout(o, gpl);
*
*   FUNCTION
*	Walks the Autodoc text buffer and builds a list of Line segments
*	with appropriate fonts, styles and offsets. Section headings such
*	as NAME, SYNOPSIS, FUNCTION, INPUTS, RESULT, EXAMPLE, NOTES, BUGS
*	and SEE ALSO are rendered in bold. The module/function header line
*	is also rendered in bold.
*
*	The scanner recognizes the Autodoc block start markers
*	"/****** ", "****** ", "/****i* " (internal) and "/****o* "
*	(obsolete), and the end marker of at least three asterisks at the
*	start of a line, per the Autodoc Style Guide.
*
*   INPUTS
*	o            - The Autodoc datatype object.
*	gpl          - A gpLayout structure with layout parameters.
*
*   RESULT
*	total        - The total number of rendered text lines.
*
*   NOTES
*	Layout runs asynchronously; the datatype signals progress using
*	DTA_Busy and DTA_Sync notifications.
*
*   BUGS
*	The module/function header detection uses the first text line after
*	the opening marker; very short files may not get a bold header.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*	Autodoc_New(), DT_MakeClass()
*
************************************************************************************************************
*
*	Private notes:
*		This file demonstrates the Autodoc format.
*		See https://wiki.amigaos.net/wiki/Autodoc_Style_Guide
*
*/